config BR2_PACKAGE_GPE_ICONS
	bool "gpe-icons"
	help
	  The shared GPE icon set (/usr/share/gpe/pixmaps/default).

	  This is data only - no code - but it is not optional for the GPE
	  apps: they all call gpe_load_icons() with a table of bare icon
	  names ("save_as", "cut", "dir-up", ...) which libgpewidget resolves
	  against this directory, and every one of them aborts at startup if
	  a single icon is missing.

	  http://gpe.linuxtogo.org/ (defunct; sourced from the Debian archive)
